    ["<Assistant_Title1>Sealed Artifact</>\n<Assistant_Title2>System Explanation: </>\nThe Sealed Artifact you are using is essentially a <Assistant_Property1>historical projection</> summoned by a mysterious \"Miracle Invoker.\" Compared to the original Sealed Artifact, this historical projection has weakened abilities, but its negative effects are also reduced, providing various boosts to Beyonders.\nAmong them, <Assistant_Property1>Ordinary Sealed Artifacts</> are divided into Attack, Defense, and Specialized types, with a maximum of one of each type equipped; <Assistant_Property2>Special Sealed Artifacts</> provide Beyonders with various special abilities and do not directly increase combat power.\n1. You can enter the Sealed Artifact system via <Assistant_System>Menu-Sealed Artifact</> or the shortcut key <Assistant_Property1>F5</> to select and equip <Assistant_Property2>Sealed Artifacts</>.\n2. Ordinary Sealed Artifacts start at level \"3\" and can be upgraded to level \"2\" by consuming <Assistant_Property1>Historical Echoes</>; they can be upgraded to level \"1\" by consuming <Assistant_Property2>Historical Crystals</>. Level \"3\" Sealed Artifacts can have up to 4 Beyonder material affix effects active, and level \"2\" Sealed Artifacts can have up to 5 Beyonder material affix effects active.\n3. When your Acting level reaches 42, you can unlock <Assistant_Property1>Beyonder material</> filling. Filling Sealed Artifacts with different Beyonder materials can attach various additional effects to them.\n4. When filling Sealed Artifacts with Beyonder materials, <Assistant_Property2>Beyonder Resonance</> effects are activated based on the number of material affixes. Increasing the Sealed Artifact level will increase the maximum number of affixes that can be activated by Beyonder Resonance.\n5. Increasing your <Assistant_Property1>Beyonder Knowledge</> level allows you to better control Beyonder powers; the effects of Sealed Artifact abilities, fixed attributes o