the Sealed Artifact level will increase the maximum number of affixes that can be activated by Beyonder Resonance.\n5. Increasing your <Assistant_Property1>Beyonder Knowledge</> level allows you to better control Beyonder powers; the effects of Sealed Artifact abilities, fixed attributes of Beyonder materials, and Beyonder Resonance attribute values will increase with your Beyonder Knowledge level.\n<Assistant_Title3>Recommended Searches: </>{SendAnswer:[Obtain Sealed Artifact]|1266}, {SendAnswer:[Upgrade Sealed Artifact]|1267}, {SendAnswer:[Beyonder Material]|1268}, {SendAnswer:[Obtain Beyonder Material]|1269}, {SendAnswer:[Beyonder Material Aggregation]|1270}",
    ["<Assistant_Title1>【Social Actions】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>System Access: </><Assistant_System>HUD - Action Button</>{JumpToUI:[【前往查看】]|1250058}\n<Assistant_Title2>Usage: </>Click the action icon to open the social action interface, then click on Solo Actions, Duo Actions, or Emotes to use them.\n<Assistant_Title2>How to Obtain: </>You can preview them in <Assistant_System>Appearance - Surroundings - Actions</> to see how to obtain them. You can also click on locked action icons in the social action panel to view acquisition methods.\n<Assistant_Title2>Sanity Impact: </>Most actions will affect your Sanity after use.\n<Assistant_Title2>Duo Actions: </>Select a target player and click a Duo Action to send an invitation; once the other party accepts, you can perform the Duo Action together.<Assistant_Red>Note: Both parties must be within a certain range to initiate a Duo Action; if the distance is too great, a prompt will appear stating it cannot be initiated.</>"] = "<Assistant_Title1>【Social Actions】</>\n<Assistant_Title2>System Access: </><Assistant_System>HUD - Action Button</>{JumpToUI:[【Go to View】]|1250058}\n<Assistant_Title2>Usage: </>Click the action icon to open the social action interface, then click on Solo Actions, Duo Actions, or Emotes to use them.\n<Assistant_Title2>How to Obtain: </>You can preview them in <Assistant_System>Appearance - Surroundings - Actions</> to see how to obtain them. You can also click on locked action icons in the social action panel to view acquisition methods.\n<Assistant_Title2>Sanity Impact: </>Most actions will affect your Sanity after use.\n<Assistant_Title2>Duo Actions: </>Select a target player and click a Duo Action to send an invitation; once the other party accepts, you can perform the Duo Action together.<Assistant_Red>Note: Both parties must be within a certain range to initiate a Duo Action; if the distance is too great, a prompt will appear stating it cannot be initiated.</>",
